{
  "name": "Track LLM prices and balance with Straitly, Slack and data tables",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "8e4b2d68-249b-4031-8ae2-48065139f3af",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -656,
        -256
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Track LLM prices and balance with Straitly, Slack and data tables\n\nKeep a daily record of Straitly catalog changes and an hourly view of prepaid balance. Slack stays quiet when there is nothing to report.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Config** holds table IDs, thresholds, the digest model and the calendar timezone. **Validate Config** rejects incomplete setup before calls run.\n2. **Read Journal** loads durable delivery state. **Read Snapshot** loads the last saved model prices, including removed entries.\n3. **Compare Catalogs** compares sorted catalog envelopes. **Build Catalog Event** finds additions, removals and price moves at or above the threshold. A first run saves a baseline.\n4. **Write Event** stores the notification before **Upsert Snapshot** changes the baseline. Pending delivery can be recovered on a same-day rerun.\n5. **Summarize Prices** returns JSON for changed catalogs. **Parse Digest** keeps a deterministic fallback and includes the raw changes.\n6. **Build Balance Event** estimates burn from the previous positive-spend interval and suppresses each sent alert type for the local calendar day.\n7. **Post Slack** sends actionable events. **Save Delivery** records success or failure; table errors use **Alert Storage Failure**.\n\n### Setup\n- [ ] Install the independent community package n8n-nodes-straitly on self-hosted n8n. It is not available on n8n Cloud until verified. Attach a Straitly API credential.\n- [ ] Attach Slack credentials and invite the bot to the chosen channel.\n- [ ] Create snapshot and journal data tables with the columns listed in the description; enter their IDs in Config.\n- [ ] Run one execution at a time. Set the workflow timezone and review both trigger schedules before activation.\n\n### Customization\n- Change priceThresholdPct to ignore small price moves.\n- Adjust lowBalanceUsd and runwayHours for your budget.\n- Change digestLimit, model and maxTokens together.\n- Archive old journal rows manually; keep today's delivery rows and the latest balance sample.",
        "width": 560,
        "height": 1208
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "f8c19a08-c592-409b-bfdb-f82d4001bcae",
      "name": "1. Start And Validate",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -48,
        -256
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1. Start And Validate\n\nTwo schedules share one configuration. Invalid table IDs or thresholds stop the execution before external calls, while the journal supplies durable delivery and balance history.",
        "width": 1448,
        "height": 704,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "90af282a-3ca8-4396-94e3-fb6906c73094",
      "name": "2. Compare Catalog",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -48,
        496
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2. Compare Catalog\n\nLoad the last active snapshot and compare sorted catalog envelopes. Exact model diffs apply percentage thresholds, preserve removed entries and make first runs a baseline.",
        "width": 1448,
        "height": 504,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "d29624a6-fb14-41e1-a521-405cccbfd777",
      "name": "3. Estimate Runway",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1416,
        496
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 3. Estimate Runway\n\nRead the USD wallet and compare it with the previous reading. Only positive spend produces runway, and sent alert types are suppressed for the local day.",
        "width": 552,
        "height": 504,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "859c3633-90d8-42f9-9f73-fa66abcb9b3b",
      "name": "4. Save Before Sending",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -48,
        1048
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 4. Save Before Sending\n\nQueue the event before updating model rows. Rehydrate the catalog event once after bulk upserts so one model catalog produces one notification rather than many.",
        "width": 1448,
        "height": 504,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "10198788-fceb-4ca6-a181-be15716c0935",
      "name": "5. Digest And Delivery",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -48,
        1600
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 5. Digest And Delivery\n\nCatalog changes get a short JSON summary with a safe text fallback. Slack delivery status stays in the journal and quiet checks end without messaging.",
        "width": 1448,
        "height": 704,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "f498d93c-c66f-48ed-bd7e-48b1ef7d5877",
      "name": "6. Visible Failures",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1416,
        1600
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 6. Visible Failures\n\nAPI or malformed response failures become durable warning events. Storage failures take a separate Slack route because the journal itself may be unavailable.",
        "width": 552,
        "height": 504,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
